        <body>
            <div xml:id="d796">

                <pb facs="0977" n="969" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg969"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.9411/130: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-28T11:00:00+03:00">April 28, 1941—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>857. The Moscow papers yesterday published telegrams sent by Matsuoka to Stalin
                    and Molotov on the occasion of the ratification of the Soviet-Japanese pact. In
                    his message to Stalin after renewing his expressions of congratulation and
                    thanks over what he described as a “Blitzkrieg” accomplished without diplomatic
                    formalities. Matsuoka said: “I believe and do not doubt that thanks to the
                    cooperation of Your Excellency, relations between Japan and the Soviet Union
                    will strengthen even more.”</p>
                <p>The press also published a joint reply from Stalin and Molotov which in addition
                    to the usual polite phrases contained the following statement: “We express the
                    firm conviction that the pact of neutrality which has entered into effect is a
                    basis for further improvement of <pb facs="0978" n="970" xml:id="pg970"/>
                    Soviet-Japanese relations the development of which the peoples of our country
                    will greet with satisfaction.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
